# PSR-4b-host-imports-close — unapproved host-source → 0

## Scope

| Work | Done |
| --- | --- |
| Classify remaining equipment import as approved settings-contract | Yes |
| Ratchet: unapproved host-source ceiling = **0** | Yes |
| Exact allowlist of approved settings-contract files | Yes (1 file) |
| Rewrite/delete `parse-equipment-icon-key.ts` | **No** (intentional keep) |
| Denali export −۹ / remove configure-* adapters | **No** (PSR-4b-exports / later) |

## Why equipment stays

[`denali-plugin-encapsulation.mdoc`](../../../dev/denali-plugin-encapsulation.mdoc):
operator settings modules export as `./settings/<module>` — **not** `./host/settings/*` —
so API settings dispatch (`parse-equipment-icon-key.ts`) stays on a stable platform
contract. Moving it under `configure-*` would mislabel a settings validator as an HTTP
product adapter.

Allowlisted path:

`apps/api/src/settings/parse-equipment-icon-key.ts`
→ `@app-tour/workspace-denali/settings/equipment-icon-registry`

## Ratchet model (after this wave)

| Bucket | Counted toward unapproved ceiling? |
| --- | --- |
| `*.generated.ts` | No |
| `*.spec.ts` / `test/` | No |
| `http/configure-*` | No (approved product adapters) |
| Approved settings-contract allowlist | No (exact set; must remain present) |
| Any other host branded import | **Yes — must be 0** |

## Metrics

| Metric | Value |
| --- | ---: |
| Unapproved host-source | **0** |
| Approved settings-contract files | **1** |
| Product defaults | **0** |

## Exit gate (host-imports train)

| Check | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Unapproved host-source = 0 | required |
| Allowlist exact (present, no extras) | required |
| Smoke + inventory metrics aligned | required |

Host-imports train is **complete** for the neutrality import gate. Remaining PSR-4 work:
export contraction (−۹), optional configure absorption, api-deps-sync.
